    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0012" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg2"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/27514: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-27T17:00:00+07:00">January 27, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 27—1:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>148. A message from our Embassy [in] London received last night stated joint
                    message from President and Churchill for Generalissimo<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d3-f1"/> was being communicated through British Ambassador<anchor
                        n="5a" xml:id="d3-f2"/> with whom by President’s direction I should arrange
                    for immediate joint delivery.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d3-f3"/> Message was not
                    received by my British colleague until this morning and we made joint delivery
                    shortly after noon. Generalissimo asked us to convey his thanks respectively to
                    President and Churchill. He made no comment. Foreign Minister<anchor n="6a"
                        xml:id="d3-f4"/> who was present said that undoubtedly Generalissimo’s reply
                    would go forward later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d3-f1" n="5" xml:id="d3-f1-content">
